For each APU instrument either a placard or colour markings or an acceptable combination must be provided to convey information on the maximum and (where applicable) minimum operating limits. Colour coding must comply with the following:
(a) Each maximum and, if applicable, minimum safe operating limit must be marked with a red radial or a red line;
(b) Each normal operating range must be marked with a green arc or green line, not extending beyond the maximum and minimum safe limits;
(c) Each precautionary operating range must be marked with a yellow arc or a yellow line; and
(d) Each APU speed range that is restricted because of excessive vibration stresses must be marked with red arcs or red lines.
